    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 14px 0;">November 2026 marks the tightening of structured address enforcement for SWIFT CBPR+ traffic. With a 10&#8211;16 week implementation timeline, institutions still in the planning phase have a latest safe start date of approximately July 2026. That window is narrowing.</p>

    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 14px 0;">Three independent regulatory bodies converge on the same conclusion. The European Payments Council mandates structured elements for SEPA, with city and country as minimum required fields. SWIFT CBPR+ designates structured addressing as best practice, with hybrid as the allowed minimum fallback — not the target state. And CPMI/BIS, through the G20 roadmap, identifies structured data as foundational to achieving speed, cost, transparency, and access targets for cross-border payments.</p>

    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 20px 0;">Three bodies. Same conclusion. <strong style="font-weight:700;">Structured is the target state. Hybrid is the floor.</strong> And by the time deadline-related urgency spikes this November — as it does every year — the implementation window for institutions that haven&#8217;t started will already be closed.</p>

