    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 14px 0;">Here&#8217;s the formula every payment operations leader should run at least once. It takes thirty seconds and the result will sharpen every subsequent budget conversation:</p>

    <!-- Formula box -->
    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin:0 0 20px 0;">
    <tr>
      <td style="background:#232F3E;padding:10px 20px;">
        <span style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FFFFFF;">Your Annual Exception Cost</span>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="background:#F8F8F8;border:1px solid #E8E8E8;border-top:none;padding:20px 24px;">
        <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:2;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 16px 0;">
          Annual Exception Cost =<br>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Annual Cross-Border Payment Volume<br>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&times; (1 &#8722; Current STP Rate)<br>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&times; Average Cost Per Exception
        </p>
        <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;color:#555555;margin:0 0 6px 0;font-style:italic;">Worked example: Mid-tier institution</p>
        <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;color:#232F3E;margin:0;">
          500,000 payments &times; 0.60 &times; $35 = <strong style="font-weight:700;color:#0972D3;">$10,500,000 per year</strong>
        </p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0 0 14px 0;">That $35 figure is the midpoint of the $25&#8211;50 per-exception range. If your institution tracks the cost more precisely — investigation time, correspondent bank charges, delayed settlement penalties — your actual number may be higher.</p>

    <p style="font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;margin:0;"><strong style="font-weight:700;">Run this calculation for your institution.</strong> I&#8217;d genuinely like to hear what number you get — hit reply and tell me. Every response helps me calibrate the data we share in this newsletter.</p>

